@title  PCSA00009 - HOLE 1 of Maple Leaf Golf Club, boot to the cup
@game   PCSA00009
@shot-every 600

# WHAT THIS RECIPE PROVES
# ----------------------
# The title boots, clears its autosave dialog, walks its whole front end, loads a course, and
# plays HOLE 1 into the cup. Every input below was found by playing, and the frames are the
# frames it was played at. The front end replays bit-identically; the ROUND does not - see the
# determinism note below, which is the most important thing in this file.
#
# THE BUG THIS RECIPE EXISTS BECAUSE OF, so nobody re-walks it: this title's input manager calls
# sceCtrlPeekBufferPositive with count = 0x20 and reads the TIMESTAMP of buf[31] - the oldest-
# first ring of the last 32 pad samples. Filling only buf[0] (correct for every title that asks
# for one sample) left buf[31] as uninitialised stack, so every press was read and DISCARDED and
# the whole front end was inert while `vitaslop::input=trace` cheerfully logged the pad being
# read. The count is a request for pad HISTORY. See vita::ctrl::fill_ctrl.
#
# WHAT WAS TRIED AND DOES NOT WORK, so it is not tried again:
#   * TOUCH. It reaches the title screen (a tap moves 6,519 bytes of guest state) but no menu
#     acts on it. The menus are pad-driven.
#   * A press held fewer frames than the gap between two pad samples: the guest samples once per
#     display frame, so a press that spans no sample is never observed at all. Every press below
#     is held at least 4 frames for that reason.
#
# HOW TO REPLAY IT:
#
#   VITASLOP_SIGNATURE=1 play --game <app> --recipe .../hole-one.recipe \
#       --shots <scratch> --max-frames 28800
#
# Both flags matter. `play` stops at 4000 frames unless told otherwise, and it computes no
# signature at all without VITASLOP_SIGNATURE=1 (it prints "sig=(not folded - no reader)"). The
# signature covers the frames that actually RAN, so a different --max-frames is a different
# number.
#
# >>> THERE IS DELIBERATELY NO @sig, AND THAT IS A FINDING, NOT AN OMISSION.
# Two replays of THIS FILE on the SAME BINARY gave sig=0x3b321b0a4814ffa3 and
# sig=0xc541cb13fe75338b. The same pair of runs truncated at f4700 - the whole front end, up to
# the tee - gave the SAME signature (0xeca9be1bdea4cf82) twice. So the boot and the menus replay
# bit-identically and something in the ROUND does not. A pinned @sig would therefore fail on a
# clean replay, which is worse than none.
#
# Note what that means for METHOD, because it is bigger than this recipe: `explore` and the
# two-run memdiff both rest on the engine being bit-deterministic across processes (the crate
# README says so in as many words, and a control variant diffing to 0 bytes is the check). That
# holds here through f4700 and does not hold through f28800. Bisecting the frame count is the
# way in.
#
# DO NOT JUDGE THE PICTURE FROM THIS RECIPE'S SHOTS. `play` renders in software, which cannot
# run a recompiled fragment program, so on this title every one of them is a flat green
# rectangle. For pictures use the headless path:
#
#   VITASLOP_HEADLESS_RECIPE=<this file> VITASLOP_HEADLESS_FRAMES=28800 \
#   VITASLOP_HEADLESS_SHOT_EVERY=20 VITASLOP_HEADLESS_SHOT_FROM=28600 \
#   vitaslop-desktop --game <app> --headless <dir>
#
# WHAT IS NOT ASSERTED, AND WHY (see the @todo at the end): no address is known for the stroke
# count or the remaining distance. `scan` for the stroke counter (u32 == 21 then == 22) and for
# the remaining distance (f32) both narrowed to ZERO candidates, so neither is stored the way
# the HUD prints it. With no signature to lean on either (above), the outcome is judged from the
# SHOTS for now - `hole1-holed-out` at f28760 shows the "+22" banner - and finding an address to
# assert on is the open task.


# The title opens on an AUTOSAVE dialog. Four presses clear it: cross, circle, cross,
# circle. Each is held ~4 frames, which is enough because the guest samples the pad once
# per display frame and this menu polls every frame. The presses are timed against the
# dialog's own fade-in. Whether an earlier press would also work was never tested - this
# is the sequence that was measured to clear it, and it clears it every replay.
420: @section autosave
420: cross
424:
440: circle
444:
460: cross
464:
480: circle
484:

# MENUS ARE PAD-DRIVEN, NOT TOUCH. Measured: a tap moves 6,519 bytes of guest state on the
# title screen and the UI never acts on it, while up/down/cross drive every screen. Do not
# rewrite these as touches.
# cross on the main menu = New Game.
900: @section new-game
900: cross
904:
1200: @shot front-end-main-menu

# cross = Single Player.
1300: @section single-player
1300: cross
1312:

# down then cross = the round mode.
1462: down
1474:
1514: cross
1526:

# cross = the course. The round that follows is at Maple Leaf Golf Club.
1726: cross
1738:

# cross = the character.
1938: cross
1950:

# square toggles HANDEDNESS. It is pressed twice - 2200 and 2512 - so the setting ends
# where it started; the pair is kept because it is what the played run did and the frame
# budget between them is what the screen needs to settle.
# start = Confirm All.
2200: @section course-settings
2200: square
2212:
2512: square
2524:
2584: start
2596:

# cross = Go to Course.
2996: cross
3008:

# cross = Start Round. The tee of HOLE 1 (par 4, 109y) is reached at about f4200.
3608: @section start-round
3608: cross
3620:
4000: @shot hole1-tee

# FROM HERE ON IT IS ONE HOLE OF GOLF, PLAYED BADLY: about 25 strokes on a par 4. The
# sequence is a proof that the title is playable end to end, not a good round.
#
# THE SHOT IS A THREE-PRESS GAUGE: cross starts the swing, cross sets the power, cross
# sets the impact. After the ball lands a banner appears ('Nice Approach!'), which needs
# its OWN cross, and only THEN does the Next Shot menu (Keep Hitting / Retry Shot / Change
# Wind and Retry / Restart / Hole Out) appear and take another cross. Getting that off by
# one press is what sent an earlier loop's club presses into the menu instead.
#
# rtrigger cycles the CLUB, and the club RESETS between shots - so every putt has to select
# the putter again (three presses: AW -> ... -> PT).
#
# POWER vs the delay between the first and second cross is CLUB-DEPENDENT and is not
# modelled: on the putter +12 frames gave 15% and +20 gave 24%, while on a wedge +12 gave
# 85%. That is why the delays below are not uniform.
4320: @section hole1-shots
4320: cross
4332:
